WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.036
Seventeen million lines

00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:02.684
of proof

00:00:03.222 --> 00:00:04.271
The recent proof

00:00:04.106 --> 00:00:04.825
of the Riemann

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.146
Hypothesis came with

00:00:05.958 --> 00:00:07.372
a startling statistic

00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:07.927
attached

00:00:08.139 --> 00:00:08.976
the proof is

00:00:08.788 --> 00:00:10.321
17 million lines

00:00:10.132 --> 00:00:10.851
of Lean

00:00:11.374 --> 00:00:12.730
Mathlib maintains a

00:00:12.541 --> 00:00:13.579
collection of over

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:14.534
a thousand famous

00:00:14.346 --> 00:00:14.994
proofs

00:00:15.053 --> 00:00:17.069
but only 259

00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:18.024
have Lean versions

00:00:17.836 --> 00:00:18.909
charted and this

00:00:18.721 --> 00:00:19.782
one dwarfs them

00:00:19.617 --> 00:00:20.171
all

00:00:20.702 --> 00:00:21.610
For scale

00:00:21.669 --> 00:00:23.355
the human-led formalization

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.015
of the famous

00:00:23.827 --> 00:00:25.277
Fermat's Last Theorem

00:00:25.089 --> 00:00:26.551
runs about 60,000

00:00:26.362 --> 00:00:26.987
lines

00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:27.671
and it is

00:00:27.483 --> 00:00:28.720
still in progress

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:30.252
Full story on

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:30.959
the dashboard
